.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAD-COUNT-EVENTS 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.73" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ead-count-events \- count audit entries without listing them
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ead count-events
[\fB\-\-user\fR|\fB\-u\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-module\fR|\fB\-m\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-command\fR|\fB\-c\fR \fINAME\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Counts the audit entries a filter matches, within the caller's own
account. The same filters
.BR euclid-cli-ead-list-events (1)
takes, and the same scope.
.PP
Worth having on its own because the answer to "how much is in here" is
often the whole question \- how far back the trail goes, whether a
retention change took effect, how busy one module has been \- and paging
through a million entries to find out is not an answer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIID\fR
Only this user.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-module " " \fINAME\fR
Only this module.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-command " " \fINAME\fR
Only this command.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
.RI ( "{count}" )
is printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
The caller was not authenticated, or does not hold
.IR ead:count-events .
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
# How much the trail holds
euclid-cli ead count-events

# How much of it is one person's
euclid-cli ead count-events --user jvo

# How often anybody has deleted a bucket
euclid-cli ead count-events --module esm --command delete-bucket
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ead (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ead-list-events (1)
